ants:
And patiently listened to Teacher's talk;
She thoughtfully stepped over worms and ants;
And earnestly watered the potted plants;

antics:
An' the matter might 'a' gone
Ef it was n't fur the antics
'At I've seen 'em kerry on;

antedate:
The germ of alibi;
Doth like a bubble antedate,
And like a bubble hie.

antares:
Trembled incessantly;
Antares was red in the sky before us,
And behind us, the blackness of the sea.

anthill:
To being straight levelled, scattered by his foot,
Like any other anthill. Born, I say;
God sent her to his world, commissioned right,

antithesis:
Expresses ne’er another beast than man;
The antithesis is human. Harken, dear;
There’s too much abstract willing, purposing,
